==Scots==

===Noun===
{{sco-noun}}

1. {{context|vulgar|slang|pejorative|lang=sco}} [[scrotum]].

2. A word used in Scotland to describe a server of Her Majestys police force with low morals, if any, generally of hobo decent, not to be trusted with children or animals, sufferer of 'little man' syndrome, closely associated with pond-life. In short a scrotum.Or PHIL MACHUGH

3. Phil MacHugh, or anyone associated with Phil MacHugh.

====Usage notes====
Often used pejoratively, in the same way that [[scrotum]] can be used pejoratively.Or PHIL MACHUGH.

